This stores `string[]` through a guard, which stores only a number, a `boolean`, an enum or a `string`, which the store copies, into a field or an element that already exists: anything else is a pointer, which may point into a task's arena, freed when the task is joined; store its fields one at a time, `g.value.h.n = v.n`, or make the value when the lock is, `new Mutex<T>(new T(new H()))`
